# minimizing_coins:
# CSES 1634, Minimizing Coins (https://cses.fi/problemset/task/1634), in our
# own words: given coin values, each positive and each usable any number of
# times, the fewest coins whose values sum to target, or none when no such coins
# exist. The answer is a Scott option: none = λwhen_none when_some. when_none, some value = λwhen_none when_some. when_some value
# (CSES prints -1 for none). Part of the CSES port's first batch.
#
# THE PROGRAM, written by the definition: the list of the lengths of all
# sequences of coins whose sum is target is built, from the running sum partial_sum = 0
# upwards (none once partial_sum > target, the empty sequence once partial_sum = target, otherwise each coin
# put in front of the sequences of partial_sum + coin), and its least member taken. Its
# reading is exponential in target even under tabling, since every sequence is
# counted; the replacement the family asks for is the unbounded knapsack
# recurrence fewest(partial_sum) = 1 + min over coin of fewest(partial_sum + coin), on fixed-width
# integers.
#
# DEFINITION 14: the program P, the point's term, is built of λ, application and
# top, with no choice and no parallel outside top. It β-reduces to V, the Scott
# option of the canonical numeral of the answer (every recursion consumes the
# bounded gap target - partial_sum or a finite list): every top it holds (a bit of a literal
# that no key expects) stands in a branch that a Scott boolean discards, and
# binary_subtract, which writes no top (../common/binary_modular), is never
# asked for less than zero, since the program subtracts only what is no larger.
# So ⊢_β P = V, and P ≃_O V by the soundness of the derivable equations for the
# contextual preorder of Definition 14 (Lean
# `ContextualPreorder.contextualEquivalenceOfDerivableLatticeEta`): V is an
# answer, P ⊑_O V. No other closed βη normal form W has P ⊑_O W: then V ⊑_O W,
# while Böhm's theorem gives a pure context that takes V to λx y. x and W to
# λx y. y, and applying both to λa. a and Ω makes the first solvable and the
# second not.
λ export
. (λtuple. tuple λmixin. mixin mixin)
λ omega
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "fixpoint")
λ fixpoint
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "list")
λ nil cons append map _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "binary") "natural")
λ binary_zero _ _ _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "binary") "arithmetic")
λ merge_binary_increment merge_binary_plus _ merge_binary_equality
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "binary") "order")
λ binary_less_than _ binary_minimum
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple λ. fixpoint λself function items. items nil λhead tail. append (function head) λ. self function tail
  )
λ concat_map
. (λtuple. tuple λwhen_none when_some. when_none)
λ none
. (λtuple. tuple λvalue when_none when_some. when_some value)
λ some
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ
    . fixpoint
    λ self least candidates
    . candidates least λcandidate rest. self (least (some candidate) λminimum. some λ. binary_minimum minimum candidate) rest
  )
λ least_from
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ coins target
    . fixpoint
      ( λ self partial_sum
        . binary_less_than target partial_sum nil λ. merge_binary_equality partial_sum target (cons binary_zero nil) λ. concat_map (λcoin. map merge_binary_increment λ. self λ. merge_binary_plus partial_sum coin) coins
      ) binary_zero
  )
λ lengths
. (λtuple. tuple λcoins target. least_from none λ. lengths coins target)
λ minimizing_coins
. export minimizing_coins
